Job Description 1

Responsibilities:

- Plan, execute, and supervise comprehensive subsurface geotechnical investigations, including soil borings, test pits, cone penetration testing (CPT), and rock coring.
- Perform laboratory and field test data interpretation to evaluate soil/rock physical and mechanical properties, shear strength, permeability, and consolidation parameters.
- Design shallow and deep foundations (spread footings, mat foundations, driven piles, bored piles, and drilled shafts) for high-rise buildings and commercial infrastructure.
- Evaluate bearing capacity, settlement (immediate and consolidation), and soil-structure interaction under static and dynamic loading conditions.
- Coordinate with structural engineering teams to provide geotechnical design parameters, spring constants, and foundation load capacities.
- Prepare comprehensive geotechnical engineering reports, design calculations, boring logs, and foundation recommendation summaries.

Minimum Qualifications:

- Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in Civil Engineering with a specialization in Geotechnical Engineering.
- 3–6 years of professional experience in geotechnical site investigation, soil mechanics, and foundation design.
- Proficiency in geotechnical analysis and finite element software such as PLAXIS 2D/3D, GeoStudio, or gINT.
- Strong knowledge of design standards and building codes including AASHTO, Eurocode 7 (EN 1997), ASTM standards, and local building codes.
- Strong understanding of subsurface stratigraphy, groundwater hydrology, and soil classification systems (USCS).

Preferred Qualifications:

- Professional Engineer (PE) or Geotechnical Engineer (GE) license.
- Experience with deep excavation shoring design and retaining wall analysis.
- Master's degree in Geotechnical Engineering or Soil Mechanics.
