- 4–8 years of experience in geotechnical earth retaining structures, slope stabilization, and excavation engineering.
- High proficiency in geotechnical design software such as SLOPE/W, Slide2/3, WALLAP, PYWALL, or PLAXIS.
- Deep understanding of lateral earth pressure theories (Rankine, Coulomb), soil-structure interaction, and drainage design.
- Strong technical writing and communication skills for preparing detailed geotechnical design memoranda and inspection reports.

Preferred Qualifications:
- Experience with soil nail wall pull-out testing and ground anchor load verification.
- Familiarity with numerical modeling of staged excavation sequences in urban environments.
- Professional Engineer (PE) registration.
