- Prepare technical specifications for ground improvement contractors and oversee quality assurance/quality control (QA/QC) during soil treatment execution.

Minimum Qualifications:
- Master’s or PhD degree in Geotechnical Engineering or Earthquake Engineering.
- 5–10 years of experience in geotechnical earthquake engineering, soil dynamics, and ground improvement design.
- Proficiency in specialized soil dynamics software such as DEEPSOIL, SHAKE2000, FLAC/FLAC3D, or PLAXIS.
- In-depth understanding of seismic design codes including ASCE 7, NEHRP provisions, Eurocode 8, and local seismic building codes.
- Proven expertise in liquefaction evaluation methodologies, cyclic mobility, and post-liquefaction residual strength analysis.

Preferred Qualifications:
- Published technical papers or specialized research in geotechnical earthquake engineering or soil dynamics.
- Experience with centrifuge testing or advanced dynamic laboratory testing (resonant column, cyclic triaxial tests).
- Professional Engineer (PE) or Structural/Geotechnical Engineer licensure.
